From f71a7046006930dbb63b47c1483a7770af5f13bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 23:05:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09286/11362] Support self-drafting MTP models, which ship
 their draft head inside the weights

Two different things are called MTP here. gemma-4-31B-it has no MTP layers in
its main weights and needs --model-draft pointed at a separate 491 MiB head. The
NVFP4 Qwen3.8-27B conversion has the head baked in, declares
qwen35.nextn_predict_layers in its own GGUF metadata, and takes --spec-type
draft-mtp ALONE.

The launcher only knew the first kind. Handed a self-drafting model it would
resolve no head, drop the MTP flags, and serve with speculation off -- shipping
a model chosen FOR speculative decoding with speculative decoding disabled, and
the only symptom a slower tok/s. That is the same silent-degradation class the
surrounding comment block already warns about, arriving from the other side.

_gguf_declares_baked_mtp reads a bounded 8 MiB from the head of the file, where
GGUF keeps its metadata, so the check costs nothing against a 23 GB model. It
matches the key SUFFIX because the prefix is the architecture string, and it
fails CLOSED: an unreadable file reports no baked MTP, which forfeits the
speedup rather than claiming speculation a model cannot do. The new branch is
checked BEFORE head resolution so a stale head left under /kaggle/input cannot
outrank a baked-in one, and it never passes --model-draft, so it cannot
reintroduce the main-weights-as-draft trap.

Verified against the real 23 GB file: baked MTP True, classified as a draft head
False. llama.cpp's own metadata reader confirms nextn_predict_layers = 1.

Also hardens the kernel's separate copy of the head filter. It used a
case-sensitive substring test, which classified Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4-MTP-HIGHEST
correctly only by the accident of upstream capitalising MTP. A lowercase rename
would have matched the only main candidate as a draft head, left gguf = None,
and killed the LLM tier silently. Now a case-insensitive prefix test, matching
_is_mtp_head_file, whose docstring already anticipated this exact model class:
a model whose name merely CONTAINS -MTP- is a self-drafting build, not a head.

5 new tests, including the bounded-scan and fail-closed paths.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
